// "Free digital signature in [state]" landing pages, 15 states chosen
// deliberately: none of them already has a page anywhere on the site
// (not in STATE_SEO_CONFIGS, not in DOCTYPE_STATE_CONFIGS), so this is
// genuinely new geographic coverage instead of a second page competing
// with an existing one for the same state. It's also the first English
// page family built around "free digital signature" at all: the existing
// FREE_FEATURE_PAGES cluster (firma-digital-gratis, etc.) is Spanish only.
//
// Every UETA citation below was verified against Justia/the state's own
// legislature site before writing (see the session that added this file
// for the source list) rather than assumed from memory. Each page follows
// the same honest-scoping rule already used for San Jose reusing
// California's real content (see city-seo-content.ts): federal law (the
// E-SIGN Act) and the state's own UETA statute apply the same to every
// signer in that state, so that part of the content is intentionally
// close across pages. What makes each page genuinely different is the
// local paragraph and the two "Local" highlights, both built from real,
// well-established facts about that state's economy, plus a fully unique
// intro and FAQ set. No content here uses a dash as a sentence break, on
// purpose, per the explicit house style for this batch.

